<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42223" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saeptĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f.
		saepio. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i>a hedging</i> or <i>fencing in</i>,
				<i>enclosing</i> (post-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5,
				12, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6,
			11</span></i> (8), 5.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, <i>an enclosing with a
				wall</i>, etc.; with <i>obj. gen.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbis,</span>”
				<i>the erection of a wall around it</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vop. Aur. 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
